@startuml physical-view-airports-routes
skinparam shadowing false
title Airports & Routes - physical view (Mode B, docker-compose.secure.yml)

node "Docker host" {
  node "edge network" {
    node "gateway-1\nnginx :8443" as G1
    node "gateway-2\nnginx :8444" as G2
  }
  node "backend network (internal, no Internet)" {
    node "keycloak-1" as K1
    node "keycloak-2" as K2
    database "keycloak-db-0/1/2\nPostgreSQL (repmgr)\nprimary + 2 standby" as KDB

    node "rabbitmq-1\nmgmt UI 127.0.0.1:15672" as RB1
    node "rabbitmq-2\nmgmt UI 127.0.0.1:15673" as RB2
    node "rabbitmq-3\nmgmt UI 127.0.0.1:15674" as RB3
    node "rabbitmq-init\n(imports definitions.json,\nexits with code 0)" as RBI

    node "airports-routes-1\nSpring Boot :8443 (HTTPS)" as AR1
    database "airports-db-1\nPostgreSQL 16\n(write + read model,\noutbox, inbox; schema by Flyway)" as DB1
    node "airports-routes-2\nSpring Boot :8443 (HTTPS)" as AR2
    database "airports-db-2\nPostgreSQL 16\n(write + read model,\noutbox, inbox; schema by Flyway)" as DB2

    node "flight-operations-1 / -2\n(each with its own database)" as FO
    node "aircraft-1 / -2\nmaintenance-1 / -2\n(REST only, no broker yet)" as OTHER
  }
}

actor "Client" as C
C --> G1 : HTTPS
C --> G2 : HTTPS (2nd entry point, client-side failover)
G1 --> AR1 : HTTPS (round-robin)
G1 --> AR2
G2 --> AR1
G2 --> AR2
G1 --> K1
G1 --> K2
K1 --> KDB : JDBC
K2 --> KDB : JDBC

AR1 --> DB1 : JDBC
AR2 --> DB2 : JDBC
AR1 --> RB1 : AMQPS :5671\n(address list: any of the 3 nodes)
AR2 --> RB2 : AMQPS :5671\n(address list: any of the 3 nodes)
FO --> RB3 : AMQPS :5671
RB1 -- RB2 : cluster
RB2 -- RB3 : cluster
RB1 -- RB3 : cluster
RBI ..> RB1 : HTTP management API\n(one-shot, at startup)

note bottom of DB1
  Database-per-Service pattern: a dedicated
  PostgreSQL instance per service instance.
  Replicas never share a database; state
  converges through AMQP events only.
  Each instance has its own outbox (replication_task)
  and inbox (processed_event); the schema is created
  by Flyway migrations (V1, V2) when the database is empty.
end note

note right of RB2
  3-node cluster, quorum queues (Raft): an
  airports.events.<node> queue keeps working with
  1 node down. AMQP only over TLS (AMQPS 5671).
  If the whole broker is down, writes still work and
  the outbox retries publication (up to 10 attempts,
  backoff min(60 s, 5 s << attempts)).
end note
@enduml
